IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wa-interpretation-nouns`

-- Interpretation Act 1984 (Western Australia) -- PART I: PRELIMINARY (ss 1 to 4).
-- s 1 (short title) and the Parts' headings are not rules.  s 2 (this Act's own day) and s 3(3) (which laws the
-- time-gated sections reach) are in wa-interpretation-time.l4, because the time rules need them.

§ `Part I -- Preliminary`

§§ `3. Application`

-- Section 3(1): the Act applies to every written law, whether enacted, passed, made or issued before or after its
-- commencement, unless in relation to a particular written law (a) express provision is made to the contrary; or
-- (b) for an Act, the intent and object of the Act or something in its subject or context is inconsistent with
-- the application; or (c) for subsidiary legislation, the intent and object of the Act under which it is made is
-- inconsistent with the application.  Whether the intent is inconsistent is a judgment the Act hands to the reader
-- of the particular law: it is a plain input.  The day the law was passed or made makes no difference to the
-- answer (it does to the sections s 3(3) gates).
-- src:116 | (1) The provisions of this Act apply to every written law, whether the law was enacted, passed, made, or issued before or after the commencement of this Act, unless in relation to a particular written law —
-- src:117 | (a) express provision is made to the contrary; or
-- src:118 | (b) in the case of an Act, the intent and object of the Act or something in the subject or context of the Act is inconsistent with such application; or
-- src:119 | (c) in the case of subsidiary legislation, the intent and object of the Act under which that subsidiary legislation is made is inconsistent with such application.
@ref s 3(1) (src:116-119)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of written law`
      `the day the law was enacted, passed, made or issued` IS A DATE
      `express provision is made to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `for an Act: its intent and object, or something in its subject or context, is inconsistent with the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `for subsidiary legislation: the intent and object of the Act under which it is made is inconsistent with the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`this Act applies to the written law` kind `the day the law was enacted, passed, made or issued` `express provision is made to the contrary` `for an Act: its intent and object, or something in its subject or context, is inconsistent with the application` `for subsidiary legislation: the intent and object of the Act under which it is made is inconsistent with the application` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `an Act` THEN
            (NOT `express provision is made to the contrary`)
        AND (NOT `for an Act: its intent and object, or something in its subject or context, is inconsistent with the application`)
    WHEN `subsidiary legislation` THEN
            (NOT `express provision is made to the contrary`)
        AND (NOT `for subsidiary legislation: the intent and object of the Act under which it is made is inconsistent with the application`)

-- Section 3(2): the provisions of this Act apply to this Act as they apply to an Act passed after this Act
-- commences.
-- src:120 | (2) The provisions of this Act apply to this Act as they apply to an Act passed after this Act commences.
@ref s 3(2) (src:120)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`this Act is treated as an Act passed after its own commencement` MEANS TRUE

§§ `4. Act binds Crown`

-- src:124 | This Act binds the Crown.
@ref s 4 (src:124)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Crown is bound by this Act` MEANS TRUE
